1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,080
The Refrigerator

2
00:00:11,919 --> 00:00:15,519
Good job! My homework is all done!

3
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:26,359
Tag! You're it!

4
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:46,300
Simka, I'm stuck! Help me!

5
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:48,300
Just stay still!

6
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:50,300
Oh, you're really stuck!

7
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:53,200
Simka, you're not going to leave me, right?

8
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:54,700
We aren't.

9
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,640
I'm afraid, Nolik, you'll be stuck for a while.

10
00:00:57,640 --> 00:01:00,359
Tom Thomas! Help me!

11
00:01:01,079 --> 00:01:02,000
What's going on?

12
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,439
Look, this blob of white stuff grabbed onto Nolik and it won't let go of him!

13
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:08,640
Oh, it's a piece of gum.

14
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:11,240
Yeah, it's my bubble gum.

15
00:01:11,439 --> 00:01:13,200
Oh, thanks a lot, Tom Thomas!

16
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:15,840
Now what's the plan to get me unstuck from here?

17
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:16,840
Here's what we do.

18
00:01:16,840 --> 00:01:18,079
It's got to be frozen.

19
00:01:18,079 --> 00:01:21,719
Once I sat on gum too and my mom put my pants in the freezer.

20
00:01:21,719 --> 00:01:24,200
The gum froze up and it came right off.

21
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:26,600
I don't want to go into the freezer!

22
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:29,280
Don't worry, Nolik. I'll stay right here with you.

23
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:31,480
Just hold on. It won't take long at all.

24
00:01:33,159 --> 00:01:34,640
Huh? Why do I need to hold on?

25
00:01:35,159 --> 00:01:37,240
The gum's already holding on to me.

26
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:44,159
Simka, do you know why it's so cold in the freezer when outside it's warm?

27
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:47,480
I'll explain it to you.

28
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:55,439
A refrigerator has a pump that pushes a special liquid through a long tube.

29
00:01:55,800 --> 00:02:00,480
Inside the refrigerator, the liquid in the tube wants to turn into a gas.

30
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:03,680
To do that, it takes the heat from everything inside

31
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:05,920
and that makes the refrigerator cool.

32
00:02:06,359 --> 00:02:10,039
Then the pump sucks in the gas and pushes it out as a hot liquid

33
00:02:10,039 --> 00:02:12,640
into the tubes on the back of the refrigerator.

34
00:02:13,439 --> 00:02:18,559
That lets all of the heat collected from the inside escape into the air outside.

35
00:02:21,319 --> 00:02:23,599
I wish I was somewhere warm.

36
00:02:23,719 --> 00:02:24,479
Hold on!

37
00:02:24,879 --> 00:02:27,000
I'll go get us some warm clothes to wear.

38
00:02:27,519 --> 00:02:28,959
I don't want to hold on.

39
00:02:29,239 --> 00:02:30,759
I want to go with you.

40
00:02:30,919 --> 00:02:32,000
Just hang in there.

41
00:02:32,079 --> 00:02:32,919
I'm hanging.

42
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,159
Tom Thomas, open up!

43
00:02:42,639 --> 00:02:44,119
Uuuuuh!

44
00:02:49,199 --> 00:02:51,919
Masiya, do we have any warm clothing to wear?

45
00:02:52,159 --> 00:02:53,679
Why in the world do you need it?

46
00:02:53,799 --> 00:02:54,839
I just do.

47
00:02:55,239 --> 00:02:57,799
Well, I need to know what is happening.

48
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:06,199
Hurray!

49
00:03:06,839 --> 00:03:10,759
Tom Thomas! Simka! Open up the door!

50
00:03:12,639 --> 00:03:17,759
It looks like I'm going to freeze up in here for good!

51
00:03:21,599 --> 00:03:25,239
A Fixie is constantly surrounded by all sorts of danger.

52
00:03:25,319 --> 00:03:29,839
Inside a dark freezer a Fixie can lose his way and freeze to death.

53
00:03:29,959 --> 00:03:33,560
If he's not paying attention he can drown inside of a washing machine

54
00:03:33,639 --> 00:03:35,399
or inside of a dishwasher.

55
00:03:35,479 --> 00:03:40,119
And a careless Fixie is always at risk of getting an electric shock.

56
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:45,840
Or suppose there's a short circuit inside of an appliance that starts a fire if this happens

57
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:49,920
You need to run away if you want to survive and what about humans?

58
00:03:50,060 --> 00:03:53,340
Well, they don't even believe that we fixies exist at all

59
00:03:53,340 --> 00:03:59,659
So they can accidentally drop something on top of a fixie or step on one or kick us across the room

60
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:01,800
So if we don't get out of the way in time

61
00:04:03,099 --> 00:04:07,200
So what I'm saying, Fixies, you need to be careful out there and pay attention.

62
00:04:07,199 --> 00:04:16,319
So be smart and stay safe, fellow Fixies! I don't understand this at all. He was right here.

63
00:04:16,319 --> 00:04:21,920
Poor Nolik! I wonder where he went. Look at this: footprints!

64
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:34,800
Nolik, you're alive! You scared me half to death! How did you get out of there? Well, you told me

65
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:36,879
about how a refrigerator works.

66
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:40,960
And so I found that cold tube and started crawling on it until it got hot,

67
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:42,120
and then I was here!

68
00:04:42,199 --> 00:04:45,680
Hey, there's smoke coming out of you! We need to cool you down right away!

69
00:04:45,759 --> 00:04:47,199
Huh? Where?

70
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:51,280
I don't want to go into the refrigerator!

71
00:04:51,280 --> 00:04:51,920
Stop!

72
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,400
I was joking!

73
00:04:54,879 --> 00:04:56,280
Look how it froze!

74
00:04:56,400 --> 00:04:58,040
I could break my teeth on it.

75
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:59,879
You aren't gonna chew it anymore!

76
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,759
I'd never do that! Not after Nolik sat on it!

77
00:05:02,759 --> 00:05:05,719
Well, you didn't need to stick it where it doesn't belong.

78
00:05:05,839 --> 00:05:08,639
Hey, I apologize. I'll go and throw it away.

79
00:05:08,759 --> 00:05:11,000
Maybe you'll try the trash can?

